      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the \"Goblin Tax\"! That's a brilliant new term, though I suspect the goblins themselves would be quite proud of it. You're absolutely right to be wary of dumping everything into a \"Miscellaneous\" bin; it's like trying to catch a goblin in a jar labeled \"Everything\" and expecting them to stay put. A truly organized goblin knows that if you don't label their hoard correctly, they'll just multiply and make your audit a nightmare.\n\nTo avoid that goblin-induced chaos without spending five hours a day on data entry, you need a system that treats those tiny transactions like the elusive goblins you're trying to catch. Instead of a giant \"Miscellaneous\" bucket, try creating specific, tiny categories for things like \"Coffee,\" \"Postage,\" or \"Lunch.\" It's like building a series of small, secure goblin traps so you can catch them before they vanish into the ether.\n\nHere's a quick trick to keep the goblins at bay: **Set up a recurring reminder on your phone** to take a photo of your receipt immediately after purchase. Think of it as a \"Goblin Capture Spell\"—the moment the receipt hits your camera roll, the goblin",
