    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the \"Goblin Reconciliation Dilemma\"! That is a classic trap, much like when a goblin sneaks into your vault after you've already locked the door, just to steal a single shiny coin and make the numbers wobble. You are absolutely right to be worried; messing up a reconciled balance is like trying to fit a whole goblin army into a shoebox labeled \"Last Month's Balance.\"\n\nThe secret to tucking these missing receipts in without triggering the \"Goblin Alarm\" (which is basically your bank telling you your balance is wrong) is to use the **\"Unreconciled Transaction\"** feature in QuickBooks. Think of it as opening a secret side door in your vault just for the goblins that slipped through the cracks.\n\nHere is the goblin-proof strategy:\n\n1.  **Don't Edit the Reconciled Transaction:** Never go back and change the amount or date of a transaction that is already marked as \"Reconciled.\" That's like trying to shrink a grown goblin back to the size of a mouse; the universe will just correct you, and your audit trail will look suspicious.\n2.  **Add as \"Unreconciled\":** Instead,",
